 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "A thousand prisoners could go home. But the biggest question stays open."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Two days of U.S.-mediated talks in Abu Dhabi ended on Wednesday. Both delegations confirmed a deal in principle on a large prisoner exchange. Ukrainian media report at least a thousand for a thousand. Russia's negotiator Vladimir Medinsky says the exact number will be set Thursday."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "On a ceasefire and territory, there was no breakthrough, U.S. mediators say. Russia still demands all of Donetsk, reports say, and Kyiv rejects that. Ukraine's David Arakhamia calls these talks among the toughest yet. Still, he sees good momentum toward a solution before year's end."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Next stop: Moscow. Jared Kushner says he and Steve Witkoff will meet Vladimir Putin, then fly to Dublin to see Volodymyr Zelensky. Medinsky says the sides moved closer to peace, and more rounds will follow soon."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will a ceasefire come before the new year? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
