 "upload": {
  "title": "Abu Dhabi Talks End. Why Is There Still No Ceasefire? #shorts",
  "description": "Two days of U.S.-mediated trilateral talks between Russia and Ukraine in Abu Dhabi ended on Wednesday, November 11, 2026. Both delegation heads, Vladimir Medinsky for Russia and Rustem Umerov for Ukraine, confirmed an agreement in principle on a large-scale prisoner exchange. Ukrainian media report an exchange of at least 1,000 for 1,000; Medinsky said the exact number would be finalised on Thursday. According to U.S. mediators, differences remain on the major issues, including territory, and there was no breakthrough on a ceasefire. According to reports, Russia continues to demand that Ukraine give up all of the Donetsk region, which Kyiv rejects. Ukrainian negotiator David Arakhamia called the round among the toughest so far, saying the Russian delegation came with strict instructions, but he also spoke of good momentum toward a solution before the end of the year. Jared Kushner said he and envoy Steve Witkoff would travel to Moscow to meet Vladimir Putin and then to Dublin to meet Volodymyr Zelensky. Medinsky told TASS the sides had moved closer to peace and that further rounds would follow soon. Timing and size of the exchange had not been officially announced at the time of production.\n\nSources:\nNBC News, Nov 11, 2026: Russia and Ukraine agree to a large prisoner exchange as talks conclude with no major breakthrough\nThe Moscow Times, Nov 11, 2026: Abu Dhabi talks end with prisoner exchange but no peace breakthrough\nInterfax-Ukraine / The New Voice of Ukraine: Arakhamia says Abu Dhabi talks among the toughest, prisoner swap agreed\nLIGA.net: What was agreed in Abu Dhabi - a large-scale prisoner exchange\nSaudi Gazette: Abu Dhabi talks end with Russia-Ukraine deal on prisoner swap\nTASS: Parties move closer to peace following talks in Abu Dhabi - Russian delegation head\n\n#geopolitics #Ukraine #Russia #AbuDhabi",
